{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5ZXkBQLbyhZKm2N7jc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `sqlmigrate` now only wraps its output in BEGIN/COMMIT when the migration is atomic **and** the database can roll back DDL (`connection.features.can_rollback_ddl`). Before, it only checked whether the migration was atomic. The migration executor already used both checks, so the two now match.\n\nThe change is one line in `django/core/management/commands/sqlmigrate.py:60`, plus an updated comment above it. The `connection` it uses is the one the command already gets for the selected database.\n\nI ran `migrations.test_commands` and all 88 tests pass. I didn't add the test the issue suggests (one that mocks `can_rollback_ddl` to False), because the task rules say not to edit test files. The existing tests don't cover the new case, so it hasn't been tested directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":220,"cache_read_input_tokens":20073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":220},"output_tokens":265,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43382385-753a-4913-b486-1726a8ac8901","uuid":"e75bf240-d481-4b9b-9c86-3432d99d92ce","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:34:54.109Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5ZXbzLJv8nCMxhkxhR"}
